  "## Status: accepted 2026-09-11 — owner chose C and its spelling (\"1, 2, 3\")

Owner instruction 2026-09-11: solve the language gaps, using subagents. This
ADR was written as `proposed` with the design and the experiment; the owner
then accepted option C with the spelling as written, in three steps: (1) the
grammar authority, (2) the vendor wave, (3) amu PR #932 and its pin.

## What landed for C

| step | repo | sha | what |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | kotoba-lang | 9c2bb949 | `guest-grammar.edn :core-form-shapes :ns` (all five clauses; `:params` new) and `:require-spec` (`:with`); `:admission-limits :max-template-parameters 8`; `surface-status :other-gaps :module-type-parameters` (`:implemented-partial`, `:implementation #{:compiler}`); digest 515bbc7d → **10ff0062** |
| 2 | kotoba-sema | e7570df5 | copy at 10ff0062; suites unchanged (nbb 388/1512/0, JVM 508/2379/0) |
| 2 | grammar | 9fe856e3 | copy at 10ff0062; `embedded` regenerated, `--check` clean |
| 2 | kotoba-lang | 1e011395 | sema and grammar deferrals removed; **kotoba's two kept**, see below |
| 3 | amu | **5cc4d826** | PR #932 merged: `module-info` admits `(:params …)` / `:with`, `link-source` keys `[namespace binding]`, one instantiation per distinct binding, refusals by name |

Re-measured at amu main 5cc4d826 after the merge: the template program links,
compiles to the SAME wasm32-browser bytes as the two hand-written modules
(sha256 d5f18eca…), and `main` answers 5. west pins advanced for all four.

## What did not close, and why — the `.cljk` rename

On the same day, kotoba-lang, kotoba-sema and grammar renamed every Clojure
source to `.cljk` (adr-2609111500). Measured by the wave agent: bare
`clojure -M:test` runs **0 tests** on all three and bare `nbb run-tests…`
fails `Could not find namespace` — pre-existing on their mains, and the only
way to measure the suites above was a symlink mirror built outside the repos.

The consequence for this wave is concrete. **kotoba's two grammar copies are
still at 515bbc7d and recorded as deferred.** kotoba's byte-identity tests
hash every guest-grammar on its classpath, INCLUDING the pinned kotoba-sema
copy; the only kotoba-sema commits at 10ff0062 are post-rename, and tools.deps
cannot load them (`Could not locate kotoba/sema.clj or kotoba/sema.cljc`).
Both variants were measured: sema pin left behind → `the classpath carries 2
different guest grammars`; sema pin advanced → the suite cannot load. The
prepared state is pushed as `wip/gg-wave-module-type-parameters-BLOCKED`
(e899e8cf) and its commit message says RED. Closing needs a `.cljk` loader on
the tools.deps classpath, or a JVM-loadable kotoba-sema at 10ff0062.

The same constraint holds amu: its kotoba-sema pin stays at 5065a9c4
(pre-rename, grammar at 515bbc7d) — a CONSISTENT lag, which is exactly the
state amu's own vendor test was designed to permit — until sema is loadable
again. `kotoba adl convert` + `kotoba doctor` therefore run against a
compiler that admits `(:params …)` but whose grammar copy predates it; this
is the shape ADR-2609101900 recorded at the repo level, now at the toolchain
level: **a rename does not fail, and the consumer goes blind.**

Fleet checker after the wave (`check-vendored-copies-fleet`, 12/12 compared):
guest-grammar in-sync at kotoba-lang / kotoba-sema / grammar, kotoba ×2
DEFERRED; two remaining findings are capability-catalog drift (amu d1452d3a,
kotoba-sema 15149f7e vs authority 9dec1e18 — the authority moved one comment
line in the rename commit). Not this wave's file; not deferred here.

## The doctor tally at amu main, for the record

Same 29-file corpus, all three kotoba-sema fixes reaching it: the
datom-source cluster has walked protocol-declaration → record-declaration →
`protocol-method: must contain one result expression` (the honest sentence);
the other classes are unchanged and still 0 of 29 admitted. `kotoba.set` is
now UNBLOCKED at the language level by this ADR's spelling — its twelve
repositories can be written once as templates — and remains blocked by the
32-item typed-set bound for datalog-sized relations, as recorded.

## What landed today (accepted, not proposed)

| repo | sha | what |
|---|---|---|
| kotoba-sema | 8b288047 | `defprotocol` / `definterface` may carry a docstring |
| kotoba-sema | 9b153c7b | the source reader reads `^meta`; `^:private` on `defn` IS `defn-` |
| kotoba-sema | 5065a9c4 | a protocol-method refusal names its cause (4 sentences, 1 code) |
| kotoba-lang | ceaf3c5d | gap records: element-type polymorphism, declaration metadata, merge-with head, reduce source, typed closure params |
